<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajendra Chola III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1246–1279</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajendra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> III was the last king of the Chola dynasty, ruling from about 1246 to 1279. He tried to restore Chola power against the Kadava chief Kopperunchinga and the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a>, at times with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> help, but was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jatavarman-sundara-pandya-i">Jatavarman Sundara Pandya I</a>. After 1279 he disappears from the record, and the Chola lands passed to the Pandyas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajendra-chola-iii.jpg" alt="Rajendra Chola III" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rajaraja3_territories2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
